<figure class="cache-figure" data-cluster-availability>
 <p class="figure-title">A copy, a majority and slot coverage answer different questions</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Failure <select data-fault aria-label="Cluster failure"><option value="none">None</option><option value="a">Primary A</option><option value="pair">Primary A and its replica</option><option value="ab">Primaries A and B</option></select></label><label><input data-full type="checkbox" checked /> Require full slot coverage</label><button data-promote>Promote A’s replica</button></div>
 <div class="cluster-topology">{['A','B','C'].map((name,i)=><div data-group={i}><div class="cluster-server" data-primary><b>Primary {name}</b><span>Online</span></div><div class="cluster-replication-link" data-link>↓ follows</div><div class="cluster-server" data-replica><b>{name}’s replica</b><span>Available copy</span></div></div>)}</div>
 <div class="cache-stat-row"><div><strong data-votes>3 / 3</strong><span>reachable primaries after this step</span></div><div><strong data-covered>3 / 3</strong><span>shards with a serving primary</span></div></div>
 <p class="cluster-command" data-result></p><p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>A simplified three-shard cluster after failure detection. Each shard starts with one replica; surviving replicas are assumed otherwise eligible. Promotion takes a separate step. Normal reads are modelled with <code>cluster-allow-reads-when-down no</code>. Turning off full coverage does not permit minority writes, repair missing data or remove election requirements. Timers, asymmetric partitions and replica migration are omitted.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{clusterAvailability}from'../../lib/caching/cluster.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cluster-availability]').forEach(root=>{const fault=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-fault]')!,full=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-full]')!;let promoted=false;const render=()=>{const s=clusterAvailability(fault.value,promoted,full.checked);root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-group]').forEach((group,i)=>{const primary=group.querySelector('[data-primary]')!,replica=group.querySelector('[data-replica]')!;primary.classList.toggle('offline',s.failedPrimary[i]);primary.querySelector('span')!.textContent=s.failedPrimary[i]?'Offline':'Online';group.querySelector('[data-link]')!.textContent=s.failedPrimary[i]?'× link down':'↓ follows';replica.classList.toggle('offline',s.failedReplica[i]);replica.classList.toggle('promoted',i===0&&s.promotion);replica.querySelector('span')!.textContent=s.failedReplica[i]?'Offline':i===0&&s.promotion?'Promoted primary':'Available copy';});root.querySelector('[data-votes]')!.textContent=`${s.connected} / 3`;root.querySelector('[data-covered]')!.textContent=`${s.covered} / 3`;root.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=`Normal GET to healthy primary C: ${s.serveHealthy?'can be served':'cluster unavailable'}`;root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-promote]')!.disabled=!s.mayPromote||s.promotion;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=!s.majority?'Only one of the three primaries remains reachable. Available replicas alone cannot supply the missing majority to authorise automatic promotion.':s.covered<3?full.checked?'The surviving primaries form a majority, but a shard is uncovered. Full coverage blocks normal queries even to C.':'C may serve its covered keys. The missing shard is still unavailable; partial service is not complete recovery.':'Every shard has a serving primary and the primary majority is reachable. This says nothing about whether every earlier write survived.';};fault.onchange=()=>{promoted=false;render();};full.onchange=render;root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-promote]')!.onclick=()=>{promoted=true;render();};render();});
</script>
